00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:23.080
episode

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:23.080
"Even if I Should

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:23.080
 Lose the Light..."

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.010
It's not a shallow wound.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:43.220
The bandages mustn't be removed until I give
the instructions to do so, understand?

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:47.070
Or else, he may become
permanently blind in one eye.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.000
Yes.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:48.700
Yes...

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:56.140
Doctor, a man can live without an eye, can't he?

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:59.980
Grandma, it's not certain he'll become blind yet.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.660
You need to stay positive.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.680
Thank you very much.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.020
See you.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.290
What happened to the Black Knight?

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.300
I'm afraid he got away.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.430
Why though? Why didn't you catch him?

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.680
After all that trouble we went through,
it was our one and only chance.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.230
Don't be ridiculous, André.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.270
How could I leave you behind and chase him?

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:32.400
It's dawn, André.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.720
I'm glad it wasn't your eye...

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.410
I really am...

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.720
André...

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:11.220
What the new era needs, aren't
hour-long speeches, but guns!

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.610
Let's go, everyone!

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:14.050
Yeah!

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.020
Attack!

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.710
What to do...

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.810
Father, is something wrong?

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.420
They've gone missing...

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:53.600
What's gone missing?

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.360
200 new guns.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.960
My subordinate was responsible for its transport.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.530
Damn Black Knight.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:11.270
Well? Do you see anything?

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:13.340
Yes.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.580
It's blurry, but a little...

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.350
Um, Doctor, what do you reckon?

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:26.410
Please open the curtains after I finish
disinfecting and bandaging his wound.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.150
Y-Yes...

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:55.810
<i>Palais-Royal...!</i>

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:00.520
Palais-Royal...

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.880
Perhaps its time I find my way in.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.730
<i>Palais-Royal.</i>

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:10.440
<i>It was the location where Oscar had once
cornered the Black Knight and lost sight of him.</i>

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:11.720
<i>Furthermore,</i>

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:15.430
<i>this grand standing structure located in the heart of Paris, was also the residence of Duke Orléans,</i>

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:18.440
<i>the King's cousin and a rumored anti-royalist.</i>

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.820
I am Brigadier Oscar François de Jarjayes.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.790
Duke Orléans has granted his
permission for an official visit.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.000
I ask that you open this gate!

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.800
Welcome, Brigadier Jarjayes.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.300
I, Orléans, welcome your visit with all my heart.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.200
Thank you.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:54.310
I am glad to see you are in fine health as always.

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:58.110
I've grown used to the shame of
being called an anti-royalist.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:01.270
So my days are, indeed, quite wonderful.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:07.150
Anyhow, please have a seat.
Formalities do not suit me.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.280
Excuse me, then.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:11.790
Let's get the business part out of the way.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.990
I hear there's something you
wish to speak to me about?

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:16.160
Yes, there's something I wish to ask you.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.120
You know the Black Knight, do you not?

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.330
I do, indeed.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.870
I've heard the rumors.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:23.770
No, not in rumors.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:25.840
As in, are you personally acquainted with him?

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.110
What an honor that would be.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.310
That I would be acquainted with
such a famous and popular figure!

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:36.280
However, I'm sorry to say
that I've yet to meet him.

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:44.260
Still, it's rather refreshing to be asked
in such a straightforward manner.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:45.440
How very like you.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:48.790
Very well.

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:52.260
Out of respect for you, I'll invite you to my salon.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:56.270
All sorts of people gather in
my salon, especially the young.

00:07:56.270 --> 00:08:01.330
This Black Knight you seek, perhaps
he's among these young people?

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.320
All the music, literature, art and academics
until now, were nothing more...

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.580
...than meaningless creations
from the salons of the court!

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:16.600
The arts and culture of the future will emerge
from salon gatherings such as ours!

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:17.390
He's right!

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.360
From the small world to the greater world!

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.560
Out from the old, musty salons
and into the sunlight!

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.460
Are you surprised?

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:29.300
My salon is open to young lawyers, artists, and
journalists, regardless of their social class.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:36.500
The outside world calls me an anti-royalist,
but I'd rather they call me a liberalist instead.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:40.250
<i>It worked.</i>

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:42.040
<i>Finding my way into this salon was my goal.</i>

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:47.330
<i>I swear I'll find the man who tried to rob
André from the vision of his left eye!</i>

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:50.420
Oh, your Latin is terrific.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.260
No, not exactly.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:55.990
By the way, the classics are nice,
but try reading Jean-Jacques Rousseau.

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:56.890
Rousseau?

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.860
He wrote the ''Discourse on
the Origin of Inequality.''

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:02.360
It clearly illustrates how the world doesn't
exist solely for the sake of the nobility.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.340
All right, capture her alive.

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.990
We'll be able to get as many guns as
we need if we threaten her father.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:11.450
Lady Jarjayes.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.400
Master Orléans has asked that you follow me.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:20.330
He said he'd like to show you
his old wine collection.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.680
This is quite impressive.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.890
So, where is Duke Orléans?

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:26.840
He'll be here shortly.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.550
Please wait for him here.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:39.660
Don't move, Regiment Commander!

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:43.060
Do as I say and I'll guarantee your life.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.790
André, do you want me to help you?

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:07.030
No, it's fine. That aside, could you tell
someone to groom Oscar's horse?

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:08.250
I doubt I'll be able to do it for a while.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:13.260
Well, speaking of which, Lady Oscar
hasn't been back for two days now.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:14.260
What?!

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:18.840
We haven't heard from her since the day
of her official visit to Palais-Royal.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:23.870
I sent a messenger, but they said
Lady Oscar left the same day.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:30.910
She went to Palais-Royal?!

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.650
How long do you intend on keeping me here?

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:41.070
Until you listen to our demands.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.700
You'll leave when you write
a letter to your father,

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.300
and we've received 500 guns
in exchange for your life.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.510
We've already looked into it.

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:52.380
Your father, General Jarjayes is
in charge of all the weaponry...

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:55.050
...and its procurement for the entire military.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:58.170
Letting 500 guns go missing is an
easy task for a man in his position.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.080
Don't underestimate me.

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:04.140
Do you really think I'd write such a letter?

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.360
In time, yes, you'll write it.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:13.060
We all know full well that the pride
of the nobility is weak and fragile.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:28.180
<i>The bandages mustn't be removed until I give
the instructions to do so, understand?</i>

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:31.290
<i>Or else, he may become permanently blind in one eye.</i>

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:44.660
Hey.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.660
H-Hey.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:50.830
Hey, wait.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:56.510
That Regiment Commander refuses
to eat the bread we give her.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:59.960
Who does she think she is?

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:02.770
Seriously, I can't stand nobles.

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:03.920
They're such snobs.

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:06.340
Yeah, they sure are.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:06.840
See you.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:06.940
See you.
See you.

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:07.570
See you.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:52.190
W-Wait, Oscar!

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:53.270
It's me, it's me!

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:55.060
André...!

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:58.030
Good lord, I was this close
to getting my neck broken.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.000
Hey, what happened?!

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.120
Who did this to you?!

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:03.560
Th-The Black Knight...

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:05.340
What?!

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.270
Wait, Oscar!

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:20.960
Someone's coming!

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:28.660
It's the Black Knight.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:29.690
Good.

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:30.680
André, give me your gun.

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:34.030
We came all this way.

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:35.060
We're taking him back with us.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:38.540
Damn it!

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:54.210
Drop your gun, Black Knight.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.250
It's my turn now.

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:03.730
Hey, Black Knight!

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:05.010
Going out to make some money?

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:07.730
Sure, I guess you could call it that.

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:08.480
Open the gate.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.720
Hey, you guys.

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:27.280
By any chance, did someone dressed as
me leave through this gate just now?

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:30.240
Ah, yes, just now...

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:31.390
What?!

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:32.490
You let him escape?!

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:33.740
He's an imposter!

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:35.710
An imposter?!

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:37.160
You idiots!

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:37.830
Open the gate!

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:38.660
I'm going after him!

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:40.160
Y-Yes!

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:54.880
All right, stop here.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:56.080
We'll wait for André.

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:00.600
Now, you too. Get off the horse.

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:03.280
And what if I refuse?

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:04.360
What?!

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:05.990
Are you going to shoot me?

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:08.820
Of course, you can't.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:10.100
I'm leaving.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:13.000
I still have a lot of things I need to do.

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:14.160
Till we meet again.

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:16.790
Stop!

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:22.080
Out of all the nobles I've seen,
you're one of the better ones.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:26.740
That's why I know you're not the type
to shoot an unarmed man from behind.

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.840
That depends on who it is!

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.350
You're the one who wounded André's eye!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:44.770
Pull something like this again and I'll
put a bullet through your left eye!

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:50.200
What's happened, Oscar?!
What was that gunshot?!

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:51.940
Did you kill him?

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.970
André, take his mask off!

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:55.480
Look at his face!

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:56.370
Got it!

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.250
He's...!

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:08.710
If I recall correctly, he's the man
who was always with Robespierre.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.230
Bernard Châtelet.

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:20.860
Born in 1760, a journalist
from Le Vieux Cordelier.

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:22.640
Such a thorough investigation.

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:25.810
If I hand you over to the authorities, I'm sure
they'll find something more interesting.

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.610
Your relationship with Palais-Royal, for instance.

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:32.680
Concentrate on getting better.

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:34.900
I'll let you stay here until your wound heals.

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:38.990
You're soft. Just as I thought.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:42.760
If you do that, you're practically
giving me an opportunity to escape.

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:44.230
I missed my aim.

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:46.290
I aimed for the top of your shoulder,

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:48.330
but the bullet went through
near your heart instead.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.800
Therefore, the doctor said
it'd be risky to move you.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:55.970
If you died from my bullet, it would
weigh on my conscience.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:57.530
That's the only reason.

00:17:57.530 --> 00:17:59.740
However, if you want to die, move all you like.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:00.760
That's your choice.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:04.680
Damn lapdog of the Queen!

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.070
A dog and a thief. I'd say we're even.

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:09.550
Being a thief is better.

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:11.020
At least a thief acts of his own accord!

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:26.920
What's wrong, André?

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.200
No, it's nothing serious...

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:31.880
My left eye is just...

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:33.340
André!

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:57.200
How many times did I say you mustn't
take off the bandages...?!

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:00.660
I'm afraid your left eye is hopeless now.

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:22.970
I'll do what you did to André!

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:40.880
Oscar.

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:42.580
I still have my right eye.

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:45.810
I can still see the rays of the sun
and the leaves on the trees.

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:49.200
Strictly speaking, I haven't lost anything yet.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:52.220
Oscar...

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:55.450
Is your heart set on turning
him over to the authorities?

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:57.300
What?!

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:00.490
Right now, it isn't the nobles who are starving.

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:01.520
It's the people.

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:04.050
There's nothing <i>we</i> can do,

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:06.970
but <i>he</i> will act for the benefit of the people.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.230
From here on, as well.

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:10.940
André, what are you saying?!

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:13.370
You would spare the man who
blinded one of your eyes?!

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:14.320
You're willing to forgive him?!

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:17.860
He's a thief!

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.410
You're right...

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:29.290
After losing an eye and impersonating the
Black Knight, I must have a screw loose...

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:33.860
I'm sorry...

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:37.880
I sometimes forget I work for a noble family...

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:54.610
Oscar!

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:55.800
Oscar!

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:00.610
Oscar, they said you did it!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:03.320
I was told you captured the Black Knight!

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.260
Well done!

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:06.570
I'm certain you'll be promoted
to Major General for this!

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:08.620
Father.

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:11.130
He was...

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:12.540
...the wrong man.

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:14.130
What?!

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:16.500
I'm afraid, it wasn't him.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:19.870
After his capture, we learned he
was just some city hoodlum.

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:22.470
No evidence was found in the subsequent
investigations, either.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:28.820
There's something I wish to know.

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:30.990
What is the relationship between
Duke Orléans and your gang?

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:32.250
He's nothing to us.

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:35.440
We took advantage of his
so-called liberalist stance,

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.990
so we could use Palais-Royal as a hiding place.

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:41.960
After all, there isn't a better hideout than there.

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:43.500
Fair enough.

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:44.950
All right, let's move on to business.

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:46.000
Business?

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:48.940
About the 200 guns you stole
from my father's troops.

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:51.970
I'll knock the price down to
1000 livres, so pay the money.

00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:53.200
What did you just say?!

00:21:57.810 --> 00:22:01.780
I've written a letter to a girl named Rosalie,
who lives in the Temple district of Paris.

00:22:01.780 --> 00:22:03.880
Once you get there, lay low for
a while and heal your wound.

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:04.970
She knows how to keep a secret.

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:06.850
Thank you.

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:09.390
I didn't expect you to let me go.

00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:12.690
If you're going to thank me,
thank André instead.

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:13.990
André?

00:22:13.990 --> 00:22:14.880
That's right.

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:19.940
In a way, perhaps he would have made
a better Black Knight than you.

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:33.120
To be continued

